## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses the ability to design data lineage and prompt hygiene features in a practical, beginner-friendly manner. It evaluates understanding of per-tenant privacy requirements and the ability to translate abstract privacy needs into concrete models and tests without requiring knowledge of large-scale system design.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant provenance tracking (input, output, model version)
- Simple redaction policy for PII detection and handling during ingestion and storage
- Lightweight policy schema and data model design
- Minimal test plan with concrete PII examples
- Data residency considerations and auditability

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal data lineage model
type LineageRecord = {
  tenantId: string;
  requestId: string;
  timestamp: Date;
  input: {
    prompt: string;
    redactedPrompt?: string;
    tokens: number;
  };
  output?: {
    response: string;
    redactedResponse?: string;
    tokens: number;
  };
  model: {
    provider: string;
    version: string;
  };
};

// Simple redaction policy
const redactionPolicy = {
  patterns: [
    { type: 'EMAIL', regex: /\b[\w.-]+@[\w.-]+\.\w+\b/g },
    { type: 'PHONE', regex: /\b\d{3}[-.]?\d{3}[-.]?\d{4}\b/g },
    { type: 'SSN', regex: /\b\d{3}-\d{2}-\d{4}\b/g },
  ],
  replacement: '[REDACTED]',
};

function redactPII(text: string): string {
  let redacted = text;
  for (const { regex } of redactionPolicy.patterns) {
    redacted = redacted.replace(regex, redactionPolicy.replacement);
  }
  return redacted;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Explores per-tenant explainability routing, privacy controls, and latency budgets in a beginner-friendly way.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant policy: explainEnabled, modelVariant, maxRationaleLength
- Request routing: explainability path vs standard path
- Latency constraints: p95 target, caching, streaming where possible
- Privacy: strip PII from explanations

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo routing sketch
function decide(tenant, prompt){
  if (policy[tenant].explainEnabled){
    return routeExplain(prompt, tenant);
  }
  return routeNormal(prompt, tenant);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you model versioning and auditing of explainability toggles? 
- What metrics and tests ensure p95 latency stays under 150 ms with explainability on?

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes ability to design real-time, scalable guardrails spanning telemetry, model routing, and incident response in multi-tenant LLM gateways, a common production pain point.

## Key Concepts
- Streaming telemetry and per-tenant baselines
- Anomaly scoring combining statistical and rule-based signals
- Remediation policies: throttle, safe-model routing, quarantine
- Auditability and drift handling across tenants
- Data locality and privacy impacts

## Code Example
```javascript
function score(latency, tokens, entropy, baseline) {
  const zLat = (latency - baseline.latency.mean) / baseline.latency.std;
  const zTok = (tokens - baseline.tokens.mean) / baseline.tokens.std;
  const zEnt = (entropy - baseline.entropy.mean) / baseline.entropy.std;
  return Math.max(0, Math.abs(zLat) + Math.abs(zTok) + Math.abs(zEnt));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you tune thresholds to minimize false positives for bursts?
- How would you validate end-to-end remediation without impacting real users?
